{"id": "EUVD-2026-96403", "enisaUuid": "3d1d21da-b695-31f8-a198-dcdf38a90525", "description": "InnoShop 0.9.2 contains a local file disclosure vulnerability that allows authenticated administrators with files_create permission to read server files by abusing the AI Core MCP file_upload tool's source argument. Attackers can supply file:// or php:// stream wrappers passed to file_get_contents(), storing contents on the public media disk to expose the .env file with APP_KEY and database credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T18:16:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:08", "baseScore": 5.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/innoshop-mcp-local-file-read", "https://github.com/innocommerce/innoshop/blob/6af6a9744414d10d2f5aab516ed0b6c3045a2848/innopacks/aicore/src/Tools/FileUploadTool.php#L55-L89", "https://github.com/innocommerce/innoshop/blob/6af6a9744414d10d2f5aab516ed0b6c3045a2848/innopacks/restapi/src/Services/UploadService.php#L33", "https://github.com/innocommerce/innoshop", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/innoshop-0.9.2-local-file-disclosure-via-ai-core-mcp-file-upload-tool"], "aliases": ["GHSA-93ww-wv4j-3wjq", "CVE-2026-108591"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ea3ade47-b69f-3bfa-9ed5-c45d702ba966", "product": {"name": "InnoShop", "vendor": {"name": "innocommerce"}}, "product_version": "0.9.2 \u22640.9.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f69f0b74-5488-3d9f-9989-c28924780c0b", "vendor": {"name": "innocommerce"}}], "isExploited": false}